~ start
Chief: Ah — Kael, isn't it? Mentor's boy.
Kael: Yes, sir. What are you doing out here?
Chief: Checking the boundary. Old habit.
Chief: You can see the whole village from this wall. Every light, every cookfire. Forty-three years I've walked this stretch.
Kael: It's peaceful.
Chief: It always is. Until it isn't.
Chief: Go on, son. Enjoy the day while it holds.
=> END
